{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ShortestSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdditiveArithmetic","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each path is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Path"},{"type":"text","text":" with the edges it takes, paired with its length. Paths are told apart by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their edges, so parallel edges give distinct paths. Paths of equal length come in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unspecified order. The out-edges and their weights are copied when the sequence is made; each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"path after the first then costs up to one shortest-path search per vertex on the path before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. Taking a prefix, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"prefix(k)"},{"type":"text","text":", gives the k shortest simple paths."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each iterator starts over from the first path. Holds a copy of the graph, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShortestPathTree"},{"text":" does.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The simple paths from a source to a target in order of length, shortest first, listed lazily","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by Yen’s algorithm with Lawler’s refinement.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/ST"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestSimplePaths","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestsimplepaths"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ShortestSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths0a6SimpleB0V","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ShortestSimplePaths.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestSimplePaths.swift#L326"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ShortestSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ShortestSimplePaths","modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestSimplePaths\/Iterator"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods",